== 1. Kinematics (equal masses): p1 - p2 vs #1's k = m v_rel/2
  (p1-p2)^2 - 4 k^2 = 0
== 2. The flag's literal comparison (both read as the amplitude-level gate, same mu)
  #6 in k: exp(-2*k**2/mu**2)   #1: exp(-k**2/mu**2)
  log(#6)/log(#1) = 2
  #6 with mu6 = sqrt2*mu, divided by #1: 1
== 3. Rate-level identity: #1 §5.1's sigma_T factor, written in p1-p2, with #1's own mu
  |#1 gate|^2 / #1 rate factor = 1
  #6 expression / #1 rate factor = 1
== 4. Overlap of two Gaussian fiber profiles, centres a separation Delta apart
     result written exp(-c Delta^2/mu^2); #6 form is c = 1/2; #1 amplitude gate is c = 1/4 (k = Delta/2)
  W1 amplitude exp(-x^2/2mu^2)  [mu = Gaussian std-parameter of psi; density std mu/sqrt2]
      O1 <psi1|psi2>: c=1/4 = #1 gate
      O2 |<psi1|psi2>|^2: c=1/2 = #6 form
      O3 density overlap: c=1/2 = #6 form
  W2 amplitude exp(-x^2/4mu^2)  [density std = mu, i.e. Delta p = mu]                  
      O1 <psi1|psi2>: c=1/8 
      O2 |<psi1|psi2>|^2: c=1/4 = #1 gate
      O3 density overlap: c=1/4 = #1 gate
  W3 amplitude exp(-x^2/mu^2)   [mu = 1/e half-width of psi; density std mu/2]         
      O1 <psi1|psi2>: c=1/2 = #6 form
      O2 |<psi1|psi2>|^2: c=1 
      O3 density overlap: c=1 
== 5. 3-D numerical check (W1, O1): exponent uses |Delta|^2 with c = 1/4
  numeric overlap = 0.7594597688; exp(-|D|^2/(4 mu^2)) = 0.7594597688
== 6. v* implied by each reading (sigma_T ~ amplitude^2; v* = 1/e point of sigma_T)
  #6 form as AMPLITUDE gate: v* = mu/m
  #6 form as RATE factor:    v* = sqrt(2)*mu/m
  #1 gate as amplitude:      v* = sqrt(2)*mu/m
== 7. #11 §8 notation: M ~ F(k^2/mu^2) and sigma_T = sigma0 F(v^2/v*^2), same F, Gaussian F(x)=exp(-a x)
  solve |F(k^2/mu^2)|^2 = F(v^2/v*^2) for v*: [sqrt(2)*mu/m]  (independent of a)
== 8. Same physical profile, two names for its width
  W1(mu1 = m v*/sqrt2) / W3(mu6 = m v*) = 1
== 9. Benchmark (#1 §5.1): m_chi = 70 MeV, v* = 120 km/s
  #1 convention mu = m v*/sqrt2 = 19.81 keV (source states ~20 keV)
  #6-amplitude convention mu = m v* = 28.02 keV (stated nowhere)
